# Keep the build context small and free of anything that must never reach an
# image: local virtualenvs, terraform state (which holds secrets), and git
# history. The image Dockerfiles copy only apps/common and apps/agent-worker.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
.env
docs/
scripts/
# The one script an image build reads: the agent-runtime-base and
# agent-runtime-browser gstack-build stages bind-mount it to check gstack's
# closure against the checked-in lists (part of #2688). Without this line the
# mount has no source and both builds fail.
!scripts/gstack_packaging_measure.py
terraform/
kubernetes/
tests/
# uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: the four control-plane builders export
# their third-party dependencies from it, by hash (#663). Ignoring it fails
# their `COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock /src/`.
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/.terraform/
# The credential file google-github-actions/auth writes into the checkout, at
# any depth. .gcloudignore already keeps it out of the Cloud Build workspace;
# this keeps it out of any other build context that starts at the repo root.
**/gha-creds-*.json
